[00:14.83]The year was 1900, 'tis worth remembering
[00:19.25]The men who lived through 55 days at Peking
[00:24.69]T'was called the Boxers Insurrection of bloody oriental war
[00:29.68]Against all nations of the diplomatic core
[00:34.10]The flags of France and Britain
[00:37.14]How they fluttered in the breeze
[00:39.66]The Italian and the Russian and the flag of the Japanese
[00:44.49]Then came the sound of bugles
[00:47.24]And the rolling drums doom
[00:49.79]And the streets of Peking were as empty as a tomb
[00:54.66]Boom-boom, boom-boom, boom-boom
[00:57.17]Boom-boom, boom-boom, boom-boom
[00:59.57]Boom-boom, boom, boom-boom
[01:02.20]Boom-boom-boom, boom-boom, boom-boom
[01:04.68]The Empress of all China gave the signal to begin
[01:09.44]And let the foreign devils be driven from Peking
[01:13.78]They stormed the French Legation
[01:16.60]They attacked with shot and shell
[01:19.07]And they came in blood red blouses
[01:21.58]Screaming shashow as they fell
[01:28.06]The drums have long been muffled
[01:30.69]The bugles cease to ring
[01:33.24]But through the ages, you can hear them echoing
[01:38.46]最可恨那毒蛇猛兽
[01:40.92]吃尽我们血肉
[01:43.38]热血已沸腾
